 {"id": "PEDS-C40-097", "sec": "JME and West syndrome", "page": 184, "q": "The diagnosis is —", "opts": ["Typical absence", "West syndrome", "JME", "Dravet syndrome"], "ans": 1, "exp": "The West triad is infantile spasms, developmental regression and hypsarrhythmia before one year. (Book p184)", "type": "case", "stem": "An 8-month-old has clusters of jack-knife spasms and repeated neck-flexion salaam spells with loss of milestones. EEG is chaotic high-voltage hypsarrhythmia."},
